258
00:15:24,290 --> 00:15:26,210
I ate a bug.

259
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:30,130
Hey, Rach. The tampons here are only a penny.

260
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:32,010
Let's stock up.

261
00:15:33,090 --> 00:15:37,390
We're out of gas and don't know where we are, so we can't get a tow truck.

262
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:41,390
- Oh. Now you want a favor?     - Yes, please.

263
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:44,100
I'm sorry your car broke down, Pheebs...

264
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:47,570
...but I'm too busy with some of my real friends right now.

265
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:50,570
But please call to let me know you got home safely.

266
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:52,650
Phoebe, hang on a second.

267
00:15:52,950 --> 00:15:54,610
Take my car. Get your friends.

268
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:56,450
No, I won't pick them up.

269
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:59,660
We both know you'll do it because you're not a jerk.

270
00:15:59,910 --> 00:16:02,870
So you can sulk here for half an hour, then go get them...

271
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:06,040
...or save time and sulk in the car.     - Rachel doesn't...

272
00:16:06,290 --> 00:16:08,460
I'm sorry Rachel dumped you for Mark...

273
00:16:08,670 --> 00:16:11,210
...and you're the innocent victim in this.

274
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:14,260
But don't punish your friends for what Rachel did.

275
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:17,890
Yeah, you're right.

276
00:16:18,510 --> 00:16:21,220
Phoebe, hang on. Ross wants to say something.

277
00:16:21,430 --> 00:16:24,140
What? You slept with someone else?

278
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:27,770
We were on a break.

279
00:16:29,230 --> 00:16:31,280
We were... Yeah.

280
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:34,570
Where are you? I'll find you.

281
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:36,280
You slept with another woman?

282
00:16:36,490 --> 00:16:39,120
Oh, you're one to talk.

283
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:45,210
Okay, done.

284
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:48,500
What's "pleh"?

285
00:16:49,670 --> 00:16:51,880
That's "help" spelled backwards...

286
00:16:52,090 --> 00:16:55,220
...so that the helicopters can read it from the air.

287
00:16:56,470 --> 00:16:59,800
Ha. What's "dufus" spelled backwards?

288
00:17:02,470 --> 00:17:03,470
Car. Car.

289
00:17:07,190 --> 00:17:09,770
Oh, it's Ross on one of his drives.

290
00:17:11,650 --> 00:17:13,530
What is he doing here?

291
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:15,650
He is saving your butt.

292
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:18,030
Unless I'm stepping on some toes here...

293
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:20,070
...in which case, I could just mosey on.

294
00:17:20,330 --> 00:17:22,790
I have plenty of people to help on the interstate.

295
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,370
- Come on.     - We need your help, please.

296
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:27,540
Fine. Fine.

297
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:35,050
Oh, no. Now it's not gonna make any sense.

298
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:38,010
You guys...

299
00:17:38,550 --> 00:17:41,510
...what do we do about Ross? He drove all the way up here.

300
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:44,020
Just send him back, then we'll go skiing?

301
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:47,140
This is horrible. It's just horrible.

302
00:17:47,770 --> 00:17:49,940
Should we ask Ross to come along?

303
00:17:50,150 --> 00:17:53,230
But what about Rachel? How are we gonna even ask her?

304
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:55,070
Ask me what?

305
00:17:57,820 --> 00:18:00,660
If, uh, it might be okay if Ross came skiing?

306
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:03,620
No, I wasn't gonna ask that.

307
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:08,750
You guys are unbelievable. No, he cannot come.

308
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,130
- Excuse me?     - It's horrible.

309
00:18:11,710 --> 00:18:16,590
Oh, please? Can't I come to your special, magical cabin?

310
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:20,510
Why would you even want to come? You're a horrible skier.

311
00:18:20,760 --> 00:18:23,550
Oh. Hitting me where it hurts. My ski skills.

312
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:25,770
Here we go again.

313
00:18:25,970 --> 00:18:27,600
I can't handle this, you guys.

314
00:18:27,810 --> 00:18:30,020
I can handle it. "Handle" is my middle name.

315
00:18:30,270 --> 00:18:33,860
Actually, it's the middle part of my first name.

316
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:37,650
All right, Pheebs, your cab's ready.

317
00:18:37,860 --> 00:18:38,860
Let's go.

318
00:18:39,570 --> 00:18:40,570
You're welcome.

319
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:44,490
I'm sorry. Were you speaking to me, or sleeping with someone else?

320
00:18:45,830 --> 00:18:47,080
We were on a break.

321
00:18:47,290 --> 00:18:50,870
Why don't you just put that on your answering machine?

322
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:53,880
It's valid, and I'm not the only one who thinks so.

323
00:18:54,090 --> 00:18:55,290
Monica agrees with me.

324
00:18:56,050 --> 00:18:57,090
What?

325
00:18:58,050 --> 00:18:59,380
I don't know.

326
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:02,090
You said it last night.

327
00:19:02,470 --> 00:19:05,760
What I said was that I understood.

328
00:19:05,970 --> 00:19:08,770
Joey is the one who agreed with you.

329
00:19:09,390 --> 00:19:10,690
Really, Joey?

330
00:19:12,270 --> 00:19:13,270
What?

331
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:17,480
You know what? There is no right or wrong here.

332
00:19:17,690 --> 00:19:20,190
I think it's very obvious who's wrong here.

333
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:22,450
Obviously not to Joey.

334
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,200
What?

335
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:31,290
- Joey and Monica feel like I do.     - You and this innocent act.

336
00:19:32,170 --> 00:19:34,330
Hey, guess who I am?

337
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:47,050
Look what you're doing to Chandler.

338
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:54,350
Look. We know that this is really, really hard for you guys.

339
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:57,360
You don't have to love each other.

340
00:19:57,570 --> 00:20:01,240
You don't even have to like each other much right now.

341
00:20:01,450 --> 00:20:04,280
But please find a way to be around each other.

342
00:20:04,490 --> 00:20:07,120
And not put us in the middle.

343
00:20:07,330 --> 00:20:12,330
Otherwise, I mean, that's just it for us hanging out together.

344
00:20:12,580 --> 00:20:14,580
Is that what you want?

345
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:18,130
Can you be civil?

346
00:20:20,090 --> 00:20:22,510
- Yeah.     - I can.

347
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:26,680
Good, let's get back in the car. It's freezing...

348
00:20:26,930 --> 00:20:28,720
...and my chest is unsupported.

349
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:30,890
Wait a second.

350
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:33,940
I mean, what are we doing? Who's going with who?

351
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:40,690
Look, you guys should go.

352
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:44,200
You know, you planned this all out...

353
00:20:45,910 --> 00:20:48,410
...and I don't wanna ruin it. So just go.

354
00:20:48,660 --> 00:20:50,700
You drove all the way up here.

355
00:20:50,950 --> 00:20:53,200
I've gotta take the car back anyway.

356
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:55,670
I'm spending all day tomorrow with Ben.

357
00:20:55,870 --> 00:21:00,040
It's fine, okay? Just go. No guilt, I promise.

358
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:02,960
Thank you.

359
00:21:05,590 --> 00:21:07,180
We'll call you when we get back.

360
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:11,060
Maybe we can, like, go to a movie or something.

361
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,770
Or the rodeo.

362
00:21:14,730 --> 00:21:16,600
- That would be great.     - Okay.

363
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:21,070
I was being Shelley Winters from The Poseidon Adventure.

364
00:21:23,110 --> 00:21:24,150
I know.

365
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:33,870
Bye.

366
00:21:58,600 --> 00:22:00,730
- Ross.     - Hi. Sorry I'm late.

367
00:22:01,110 --> 00:22:03,440
- Were you sleeping?     - Uh, no.

368
00:22:03,610 --> 00:22:04,980
Oh, great.

369
00:22:06,150 --> 00:22:09,450
I had to get you a new battery. I got the best I could.

370
00:22:09,660 --> 00:22:11,490
You don't want to skimp there.

371
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:12,830
You're a genius.

372
00:22:13,080 --> 00:22:14,540
It came to about $112.

373
00:22:14,790 --> 00:22:17,160
But what the hell, call it an even 110?

374
00:22:18,580 --> 00:22:20,620
I'll pay you tomorrow. Bye.

375
00:22:20,830 --> 00:22:23,290
So they, uh, all took off.

376
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:26,630
It was pretty hard watching them go, you know?

377
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,470
Yeah, okay. Bye.

378
00:22:32,510 --> 00:22:34,760
So I'm gonna take off then.

